SEQUENCE:1780758994
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260608
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260609
SUMMARY:Upper Strength + Calisthenics Pull
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3350 kcal\, 175 g protein\, 455 g carbs\, 9
 5 g fat\nMacro timing: 35-45 g protein in 4 meals\, 40-70 g carbs before 
 lifting\, and a protein-plus-carb meal after training.\nCategory: gym\nRu
 n volume: 0 km\nAdjustments:\n- Adjusted for recovery constraint.\n\nWarm
 -Up:\n- 5-7 min easy bike\, band pull-aparts\, scap push-ups\, and 2 benc
 h ramp sets.\n\nMain Work:\n- Progression: double progression\; add load 
 only after all sets reach the top of the range at RPE 8 or lower\, about 
 2 RIR. Recovery constraint: avoid impact\, fast push-off\, and exercises 
 that worsen next-morning symptoms.\n- Bench press: top set 1 x 4-6 at RPE
  8\, then 3 back-off sets x 5-7 at RPE 7-8.\n- Pull-ups: 4 x 4-8 at RPE 8
  paired with chest-supported row 4 x 8-12 at RPE 8.\n- Overhead press or 
 Arnold press: 3 x 6-10 at RPE 8 paired with incline dumbbell press or dum
 bbell press 2 x 8-10 at RPE 8.\n- Shoulder and arm finisher: lateral rais
 es 3 x 12-20 at RPE 8 plus farmer carries 4 x 30-40 m\, preacher curls or
  hammer curls 2 x 10-15\, and reverse curls 2 x 12-15.\n\nFueling:\n- Hit
  daily macros\, keep protein near target\, and place carbohydrates before
  and after training.\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; add
  mobility if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
