SUMMARY:Lower Strength + Knee Capacity
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3500 kcal\, 180 g protein\, 505 g carbs\, 1
 00 g fat\nMacro timing: hit the higher protein target with 40-45 g protei
 n in 4 meals\, plus 50-80 g carbs before heavy lifting and carbs again af
 ter.\nCategory: gym\nRun volume: 0 km\nAdjustments:\n- Adjusted for recov
 ery constraint.\n\nWarm-Up:\n- 7-8 min bike\, ankle rocks\, bodyweight sq
 uats\, and short-foot activation.\n\nMain Work:\n- Progression: double pr
 ogression\; add load only when knee tracking stays clean\, discomfort sta
 ys 0-2/10\, and top sets stay near RPE 8. Recovery constraint: avoid impa
 ct\, fast push-off\, and exercises that worsen next-morning symptoms.\n- 
 Hack squat or goblet squat: top set 1 x 6-8 at RPE 8\, then 3 back-off se
 ts x 8-10 at RPE 7-8.\n- Romanian deadlift: 4 x 6-8 at RPE 7-8 with contr
 olled eccentrics.\n- Leg press or hack squat: 3 x 8-12 at RPE 7-8 with st
 able foot pressure and no symptom increase.\n- Lower-leg rehab: foot-intr
 insic activation\, short-foot / arch lifts\, gentle inversion isometrics\
 , sole-to-sole isometrics\, and double-leg heel raise isometric holds.\n\
 nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein near target\, and place carb
 ohydrates before and after training.\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 2
 2:00-06:00\; add mobility if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
