SUMMARY:Legs + Delts Accessory
DESCRIPTION:Overview:\nMacros: 3350 kcal\, 175 g protein\, 455 g carbs\, 9
 5 g fat\nMacro timing: 35-45 g protein in 4 meals\, 40-70 g carbs before 
 lifting\, and a protein-plus-carb meal after training.\nCategory: gym\nRu
 n volume: 0 km\nAdjustments:\n- Adjusted for recovery constraint.\n\nWarm
 -Up:\n- 5-6 min easy bike\, ankle rocks\, band pull-aparts\, and one ramp
  set for each pairing.\n\nMain Work:\n- Progression: keep this short and 
 low-fatigue\; stop 1-2 reps before failure and leave fresher than you arr
 ived. Recovery constraint: avoid impact\, fast push-off\, and exercises t
 hat worsen next-morning symptoms.\n- Leg extension: 3 x 12-18 at RPE 8 pa
 ired with seated or lying hamstring curl 3 x 10-15 at RPE 8.\n- Lower-leg
  rehab: foot-intrinsic activation\, short-foot / arch lifts\, gentle inve
 rsion isometrics\, sole-to-sole isometrics\, and double-leg heel raise is
 ometric holds.\n- Rear delt fly or reverse pec-deck: 2-3 x 15-20 at RPE 8
 \; if time is tight\, complete the first 3 exercises and leave.\n- Chest/
 back/core top-up: push-ups 2 x clean reps\, dips 2 x 6-10\, cable row 2 x
  10-12\, face pulls 2 x 12-15\, Pallof press 3 x 10 per side\, plank vari
 ations 2 x 30-45 sec\, kettlebell side bend 2 x 10-12\, around the head k
 ettlebell 2 x 8 each way\, and weighted sit-ups 2 x 8-12.\n\nFueling:\n- 
 Hit daily macros\, keep protein near target\, and place carbohydrates bef
 ore and after training.\n\nRecovery:\n- Sleep window stays 22:00-06:00\; 
 add mobility if joints feel stiff.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
