 n volume: 0 km\nAdjustments:\n- Adjusted for recovery constraint.\n\nWarm
 -Up:\n- 5 min easy cardio\, shoulder prep\, light rows\, and thoracic mob
 ility.\n\nMain Work:\n- Progression: double progression\; add reps before
  load and keep the whole session capped around RPE 8. Recovery constraint
 : avoid impact\, fast push-off\, and exercises that worsen next-morning s
 ymptoms.\n- Chest-supported row\, cable row\, Pendlay row\, or barbell ro
 w: 4 x 8-12 at RPE 8 paired with dumbbell or machine shoulder press 3 x 8
 -10 at RPE 8.\n- Lat pull-down or pull-ups: 3 x 8-12 at RPE 8 paired with
  incline dumbbell press 2-3 x 8-12 at RPE 8.\n- Shoulder and upper back f
 inisher: lateral raises 3 x 15-20\, rear delt fly or reverse pec-deck 3 x
  15-20\, face pulls 2 x 12-15\, and dumbbell rotator cuff work.\n- Bike s
 ubstitute: 20-35 min easy bike or walk 20-30 min on flat ground if sympto
 m-free.\n\nFueling:\n- Hit daily macros\, keep protein near target\, and 
